    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "NE 0, SEA 0",
        "text": "Dre'Mont Jones sacked Sam Darnold on third down to end Seattle's opening drive, and Darnold came up limping with a hip injury and went to the locker room. Drew Lock took over, and neither team scored."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "NE 7, SEA 0",
        "text": "A pass interference call on Josh Jobe, covering A.J. Brown on a deep flea-flicker, set up Drake Maye's 2-yard touchdown pass to rookie tight end Eli Raridon on the next play (7–0 with 9:11 left in the half). It was the only score of the first half."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "NE 10, SEA 3",
        "text": "A roughing-the-punter penalty on Chazz Surratt set up Andy Borregales' 50-yard field goal on New England's first drive of the half for a 10–0 lead. Jason Myers answered with a 30-yarder (10–3), and Brown left with a right ankle injury and did not return."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: SEA 13, NE 10",
        "text": "Maye threw three interceptions in the quarter. Nehemiah Pritchett's pick with 14:27 left started the comeback, and Lock hit Jaxon Smith-Njigba for a 45-yard touchdown on fourth-and-1 to tie it 10–10 with 11:28 left. Julian Love picked Maye off on the next drive and Myers' 26-yard field goal made it 13–10 with 5:50 left; Maye drove New England into range in the final minute, but Jobe made a toe-tapping interception in the end zone with 26 seconds left."
      }
    ],
